  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run it or look at a rendered frame, so the look, light intensities and camera framing are untested. I also didn't run `vite build`.\n\n- **Floor:** A seamless light-grey floor curves up into the backdrop. I generated the geometry in code with `geometry.define`.\n- **Spheres:** Three equal spheres (diameter 1.7) sit in a row.\n  - **Left, glass:** `material.clearGlass` with transmission, a slight tint, IOR 1.5 and strong environment reflections.\n  - **Centre, brushed metal:** `material.brushedMetal`, fully metallic, with anisotropic stretched reflections and the brushed procedural texture.\n  - **Right, fabric:** dark red `material.fabric`, fully rough, with a sheen lobe and a fine procedural weave normal.\n- **Lights:** A key directional light with soft PCSS shadows moves side to side. A dimmer fill comes from the opposite side and a rim light from behind. A fixed rectangular softbox gives a rectangular highlight on the glass and metal. The studio environment gives the metal and glass something to reflect, and screen-space contact shadows are on.\n- **Camera:** Fixed and slightly raised at a three-quarter-front angle, aimed at the centre of the row.\n- **Animation:** The key light sweeps along x as a sine wave, about 16.5 s per cycle, updated every frame. `window.__TASK_STATE__` carries the three sphere names and the live `keyLightX`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nThe softbox does not move with the key light. I wasn't sure it would re-aim when repositioned, so the moving highlights come from the key directional light.\n\n",
